    "editorial": {
      "title": "MongoDB catch-up flaw reaches replica sets before authentication",
      "summary": "MongoDB disclosed CVE-2026-118383 on November 10. The replication use-after-free affects replica set members, including shard and config-server members; standalone instances are outside its scope. Datadog reproduced a crash, while the advisory also describes possible code execution.",
      "why_it_matters": "Authentication alone does not stop the triggering requests. The catch-up condition matters; a reproduced crash does not prove reliable RCE or attacks in the wild.",
      "action": "Upgrade every affected replica set member to its branch’s fixed release. Datadog lists 8.0.37 for the 8.0 branch; restrict network access while completing the rollout.",
